BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
LOCATION:Doyle Library\, 1st Floor Lobby - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:In the Spotlight: Lawrence's George "Nash" Walker
DESCRIPTION:Featuring the research and personal collection of author Dani
 el Atkinson\, In the Spotlight: Lawrence's George "Nash" Walker follows t
 he career of George "Nash" Walker from Lawrence\, Kansas to the lights of
  Broadway.&#160\;  Walker and his partner\, Bert Williams\, performed a h
 ighly successful vaudeville act on Broadway and overseas\, blazing a trai
 l of opportunity for future Black actors and actresses.This exhibit is fu
 nded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Ne
 wman Cultural Endowment.For more information\, visit the SRJC Multicultur
 al Museum Website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/spotlight-george-n
 ash-walker)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Featuring the research and personal col
 lection of author Daniel Atkinson\, <em>In the Spotlight: Lawrence's Geor
 ge "Nash" Walker</em> follows the career of George "Nash" Walker from Law
 rence\, Kansas to the lights of Broadway.&#160\;</p><p>  Walker and his p
 artner\, Bert Williams\, performed a highly successful vaudeville act on 
 Broadway and overseas\, blazing a trail of opportunity for future Black a
 ctors and actresses.<br /><br /><em>This exhibit is funded by a grant fro
 m the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Endow
 ment.</em></p><p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/spotlight-ge
 orge-nash-walker" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\, v
 isit the SRJC Multicultural Museum Website.</a></p>
